sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / kubectl
    participant APIServer as kube-apiserver<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Webhook as Admission Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Operator as ModelRegistryReconciler<br/>ServiceAccount token
    participant Template as TemplateApplier<br/>go:embed YAML
    participant Registry as Model Registry Pod<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant KRBAC as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP

    Note over User,DB: Flow 1: Model Registry Instance Deployment

    User->>APIServer: POST ModelRegistry CR<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    APIServer->>Webhook: Admission Review<br/>TLS
    Webhook-->>APIServer: Mutated + Validated CR
    APIServer-->>User: CR Created

    Operator->>APIServer: Watch ModelRegistry CRs<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
    APIServer-->>Operator: ModelRegistry event

    Operator->>Template: Render templates<br/>(DB type, auth mode, features)
    Template-->>Operator: Rendered YAML resources

    Operator->>APIServer: Create Deployment, Service,<br/>Secret, RBAC, NetworkPolicy
    Operator->>APIServer: Create Route / HTTPRoute<br/>(if OpenShift / Gateway API)

    Note over User,DB: Flow 2: Model Registry API Access (kube-rbac-proxy mode)

    participant Client as API Client

    Client->>Route: GET /api/model_registry/v1alpha3/...<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    Route->>KRBAC: Forward (re-encrypt TLS)<br/>:8443/TCP
    KRBAC->>APIServer: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    APIServer-->>KRBAC: Auth result (allowed/denied)
    KRBAC->>Registry: Forward to localhost<br/>:8080/TCP HTTP (pre-authorized)
    Registry->>DB: Query metadata<br/>:5432/TCP, Credentials Secret
    DB-->>Registry: Query results
    Registry-->>KRBAC: JSON response
    KRBAC-->>Route: Encrypted response
    Route-->>Client: JSON Response
